NAME
       nohup - run a command that keeps going after you log out

SYNOPSIS
       nohup COMMAND [ARGUMENT...]

DESCRIPTION
       When you log out, the shell sends the hang-up signal (SIGHUP) to the
       programs it started, and most of them end. nohup starts COMMAND so
       that it ignores this signal. Output that would go to the terminal is
       written to nohup.out in the current directory (or in your home
       directory) instead.

       Add & to run it in the background.

EXAMPLES
           nohup ./long-job.sh &
           nohup tar -czf /root/home.tgz /home > /root/tar.log 2>&1 &

SEE ALSO
       bash(1), jobs(1), disown(1), at(1), systemd-run(1)
